  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 3, 10, 'canon', 'proverbs', 6, 25, 'free', E'Proverbs 6:25 — *Lust not after her beauty in thine heart; neither let her take thee with her eyelids.* — the warning to "pay no heed to the face of a woman" is Solomon''s counsel against the strange woman word for word.')
