       E'Thou shalt stand near the Lord and be His minister',
       E'The angel tells Levi that when he ascends he shall stand near the Lord, be His minister, declare His mysteries, and proclaim the One who shall redeem Israel — and that by Levi and by Judah the Lord shall appear among men. This is the joined hope of the two tribes, the priest of Levi and the king of Judah, from whom salvation arises. It ain''t new — the Star of Jacob and the priest who stands before the Lord are already spoken in Moses and the Prophets.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 87428
  FROM _session413_t18_lookup sv, _session413_t18_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='pseudepigrapha' AND sv.book_slug='testaments-xii' AND sv.chapter_number=18 AND sv.verse_number=10
   AND ev.edition_slug='pseudepigrapha' AND ev.book_slug='testaments-xii' AND ev.chapter_number=18 AND ev.verse_number=11
