  -- thread: testaments-xii-24-seven-men-in-white-anoint-the-priest
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 24, 2, 'canon', 'exodus', 28, 4, 'free', E'Exodus 28:4 — *a breastplate, and an ephod, and a robe, and a broidered coat, a mitre, and a girdle: and they shall make holy garments.* The robe, breastplate, ephod, and turban put upon Levi are the very holy garments Moses commanded for the priest.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 24, 4, 'canon', 'exodus', 29, 7, 'free', E'Exodus 29:7 — *Then shalt thou take the anointing oil, and pour it upon his head, and anoint him.* The first man anointing Levi with holy oil is Aaron''s anointing in the Torah.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 24, 5, 'canon', 'exodus', 29, 4, 'free', E'Exodus 29:4 — *And Aaron and his sons thou shalt bring unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shalt wash them with water.* The second washing Levi with pure water is the washing of the priest at his consecration.'),
