  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 25, 4, 'canon', 'genesis', 28, 22, 'free', E'Genesis 28:22 — *of all that thou shalt give me I will surely give the tenth unto thee.* Jacob paying tithes at Bethel through Levi fulfils his own Bethel vow of the tenth.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 25, 4, 'canon', 'numbers', 18, 6, 'free', E'Numbers 18:6 — *I have taken your brethren the Levites... to do the service of the tabernacle.* That Jacob renders the tithe ''through me,'' Levi, is the Levites set apart to the service the tithe sustains.'),
  -- thread: testaments-xii-25-the-law-of-the-priesthood-and-clean-offerings
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 25, 13, 'canon', 'leviticus', 11, 47, 'free', E'Leviticus 11:47 — *To make a difference between the unclean and the clean, and between the beast that may be eaten and the beast that may not be eaten.* Offering ''of every clean beast and bird'' keeps the Torah''s distinction of clean and unclean.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 25, 14, 'canon', 'leviticus', 2, 13, 'free', E'Leviticus 2:13 — *with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt.* ''Every sacrifice thou shalt salt with salt'' is the covenant of salt commanded in the law.')
)
