       E'Er and Onan — slain for their wickedness against Tamar',
       E'Judah recounts how his firstborn Er took Tamar, was wicked, and was smitten; and how Onan, refusing to raise up seed, spilled it on the ground and likewise died. It ain''t new — Moses set down both deaths word for word, and the Torah''s law of raising seed to a brother stands behind the whole account.',
