  -- thread: testaments-xii-75-clothed-the-naked-in-winter
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 75, 1, 'canon', 'matthew', 25, 36, 'free', E'Matthew 25:36 — *Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.* Zebulun clothing the naked man in winter is the very deed the King receives as done to himself.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 75, 2, 'canon', 'leviticus', 19, 18, 'free', E'Leviticus 19:18 — *but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am Yahuah (LORD).* Showing compassion and mercy without hesitation to all men is the love of neighbour Torah lays as the rule.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 75, 3, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 29, 8, 'free', E'Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 29:8 — *Yet have you patience with a man in poor estate, and delay not to shew him mercy.* Where Zebulun had nothing to give yet kept compassion in bowels of mercy, he keeps the fathers'' word to show mercy even in want.')
