  -- thread: testaments-xii-77-divided-into-two-kingdoms
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 5, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 22, 'free', E'Ezekiel 37:22 — *And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Yashar''el (Israel); and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.* Zebulun''s "ye shall be divided... and follow two kings" is the very division of the two kingdoms Ezekiel says shall at last be made one.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 4, 'canon', 'ezekiel', 37, 17, 'free', E'Ezekiel 37:17 — *And join them one to another into one stick; and they shall become one in thine hand.* That everything Yahuah made has but one head is mirrored in the two sticks of Judah and Joseph made one in Yahuah''s hand.'),
  -- thread: testaments-xii-77-led-captive-then-mercy
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 7, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 2, 'free', E'Deuteronomy 30:2 — *And shalt return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart, and with all thy soul.* "Ye shall remember Yahuah and repent, and He shall have mercy" is the return with all the heart Moses foretold.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 7, 'canon', 'deuteronomy', 30, 3, 'free', E'Deuteronomy 30:3 — *That then Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God) hath scattered thee.* Yahuah being merciful and compassionate to the repentant captives is Moses'' promise to turn the captivity and gather them.'),
  -- thread: testaments-xii-77-the-light-of-righteousness-shall-arise
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 8, 'canon', 'malachi', 4, 2, 'free', E'Malachi 4:2 — *But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.* "Yahuah Himself, the light of righteousness" rising upon them is the Sun of righteousness Malachi says shall arise with healing.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 8, 'canon', 'isaiah', 9, 2, 'free', E'Isaiah 9:2 — *The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.* The light of righteousness arising upon Israel is the great light Isaiah says shall shine on the people in darkness — the land of Zebulun named in the verses before.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 8, 'canon', 'isaiah', 60, 1, 'free', E'Isaiah 60:1 — *Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of Yahuah (LORD) is risen upon thee.* That ye shall see Him in Jerusalem when the light arises is the glory of Yahuah risen upon Zion as her sons are gathered.'),
  ('pseudepigrapha', 'testaments-xii', 77, 8, 'canon', 'ephesians', 4, 8, 'free', E'Ephesians 4:8 — *Wherefore he saith, When he ascended up on high, he led captivity captive, and gave gifts unto men.* Yahuah Himself arising and bringing them back from captivity to their own land is the captivity-led-captive the apostle proclaims in the Messiah.')
