       E'Dying Dan presses one charge home: keep yourselves from lying and anger and love truth and longsuffering, or you perish, for anger is a blindness that lets a man see no father, brother, prophet, or friend, and ends in hatred and envy. The apostles preach the cure in the same breath — be swift to hear, slow to wrath, longsuffering, putting away bitterness. It ain''t new: wrath blinds, but the slow-to-anger walk in great understanding.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 88975
