SELECT 'testaments-xii-91-the-ship-of-jacob-scattered-and-regathered',
       E'The ship of Jacob — scattered to the ends of the earth, gathered in peace',
       E'In a second dream the ship of Jacob is broken up in a tempest and all the sons are scattered unto the ends of the earth — yet Levi and Judah are together, Levi prays in sackcloth for them all, and when the storm ceases the ship reaches land in peace and the father returns and all rejoice. The figure is the scattering and gathering of Israel, kept by the joined priest and king. It ain''t new — Moses foretold the driving to the outmost parts of heaven and the gathering home, and Ezekiel the reuniting of the two houses into one.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 89250
