       E'Hatred will not hear the commandment concerning loving one''s neighbour',
       E'Gad warns that hatred worketh lawlessness even against the Lord, for it will not hear His commandments concerning the loving of one''s neighbour. He names the precise Torah word it refuses — the command to love thy neighbour as thyself. It ain''t new — the lawlessness of hatred is measured against the very statute Moses gave.',
