       E'Men of single face — just before God, like the clean stag and hind',
       E'Asher turns to the good men of single face: though the double-faced think they sin, they are just before God; they are like stags and hinds, which seem wild and unclean but are altogether clean, because they walk in zeal for the Lord and abstain from what God hateth and forbiddeth by His commandments. The single face is the single eye that fills the whole body with light, and the clean creature is read straight off Torah''s law of clean and unclean. It ain''t new — the single-faced man Asher commends keeps the very commandments of God that mark clean from unclean.',
