       E'Asher''s own walk — singleness of face, searching out the commandments',
       E'Asher closes his teaching on the two by witnessing to his own life: he proved all these things, wandered not from the truth of the Lord, and searched out the commandments of the Most High, walking with singleness of face unto good. The man who keeps one face is the doer who looks into the perfect law of liberty and continues in it, blessed in his deed. It ain''t new — Asher''s singleness of face is a life spent searching out and keeping the commandments, the doer''s path the apostle commends.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 89650
  FROM _session413_t107_lookup sv, _session413_t107_lookup ev
