       E'The bloodied coat and the brother sold to the Ishmaelites',
       E'Joseph tells Benjamin what the brothers reported to Jacob — that they dipped the coat in blood — and what they truly did: stripped him of it and gave him to the Ishmaelites. The testament simply gives Joseph''s voice to the deeds Moses records. It ain''t new — the dabbled coat and the selling are the Torah''s own account of the wrong Joseph would later forgive.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 90275
